{"name":"Soar","hex":"#ddf0f0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Soar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in Leicestershire, England, a tributary to the Trent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Soar"}],"entries":[{"title":"160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment (Airborne)","blocks":[{"text":"The 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment (Airborne), abbreviated as 160th SOAR(A), is a special operations force of the United States Army that provides helicopter aviation support for special operations forces. Its missions have included attack, assault, and reconnaissance, and these missions are usually conducted at night, at high speeds, low altitudes, and on short notice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/160th_SOAR_emblem.svg/330px-160th_SOAR_emblem.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/160th_Special_Operations_Aviation_Regiment_(Airborne)"},{"title":"Safe operating area","blocks":[{"text":"For power semiconductor devices, the safe operating area (SOA) is defined as the voltage and current conditions over which the device can be expected to operate without self-damage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/BDV66C_limits.png/330px-BDV66C_limits.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safe_operating_area"},{"title":"Soar (cognitive architecture)","blocks":[{"text":"Soar is a cognitive architecture, originally created by John Laird, Allen Newell, and Paul Rosenbloom at Carnegie Mellon University."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soar_(cognitive_architecture)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/US_Army_160th_SOAR%28A%29_CH-47_sling-load_a_Mi-24_out_of_Chad-Operation_Mount_Hope_III.jpg/500px-US_Army_160th_SOAR%28A%29_CH-47_sling-load_a_Mi-24_out